{
  "_doc": "The Krai Warhost's hull texture designs (change hull-texture-designs, mockup 24): the frigate's detail layer and paint, built by tools/blender/hull_detail.py and baked by tools/blender/painted_bake.py --detail data/ships/krai/hull_detail.json --ship krai_k1,... onto the frigate's own UVs. The mesh is the game's model (tools/mockups/glb_hull_obj.py, in its export frame); the room plan (data/ships/krai/frigate_plan.json) sits 25.93 m forward of it. The story (where the ship's rooms put its vents, its boarding bay, its gun and its drives) is shared by every design; a design is its plating, its paint and how it wears. Each design names the tradition it comes from (CLAUDE.md section 1). Nothing round (the Krai cut, they do not turn): vents are slots and chevrons, no domes or fans. The frigate's window slits are the model's own.",
